/* book exam traps: Use VSB = VS − VB under the root, positive for reverse bias in an nMOS. Putting in VBS = −1 V gives √(2φF − 1), which is not even real when 2φF < 1 V. | The formula has 2φF, not φF, in both the bending term and the square roots. | γ has units √V; γ × √V gives volts. | Keep NA in m⁻³ with q, εsi and Cox in SI units; mixing cm⁻³ in gives answers off by 10³. | Body effect is zero only when source and body are at the same voltage; in a stack, only the bottom transistor is free of it. */
